brief about tinyterm7

	note, the tool tinyterm7 is only intended to provide network connection 
	to original "minix 3 book" image running in remote virtual environment
	with minix VGA console look and feel

	as minix around, tinyterm7 also is trying to deal with minimal balanced preset 
	of termcap strings, there are no extra termcap features supported

	tinyterm7 a little extends minix VGA console with rollback buf, alt screen and mouse, 
	so other apps can also run in tinyterm7 with colors and mouse, 
	but tinyterm7 is not going to be xterm terminal, check your apps to agree with 
	tinyterm7 if you want to work in tinyterm7 better
		
		there are differences with xterm, for example work of mouse modes Mx or alt screen; 
		tinyterm7 does not switch to alt screen, but similar to save cursor_pos 
		do internal copy of { screen, cursor and color attr }, so you can join own data
		with current screen (partially draw own files panel for example) 
		and later anytime can restore backround from saved screen copy (remove 
		own panels from screen) 

	from app point of view, tinyterm7 is contolled by set of tty commands
	termcap and terminfo are sources of tinyterm7 tty commands
		mx1.cap
		mx1.ti
	compile terminfo binary by "tic -a -x -N -T -U -r mx1.ti"
	set terminal name by "export TERM=mx1"

other differences
	'ctlr+letter' control code mapped to ctlr+shift+letter key area, 
	ut us possible to use ctrl+c and ctrl+v as in GUI

	esc key mapped to CAN (^X), use ctlr+shift+[ or ESC+key to get ESC, 
	it is assumed you will learn apps to read ^X instead of looking for ESC in keyboard

	because of Windows keyboard default behaviour, alt+ is not set for 9_keys_of_keypad 
	in favor of alt+digit composed codes, that is not a problem in GUI point of view

new minix terminal properties

	added "clear in line", some easy set/reset modes 

	removed boolean data that now has set/reset strings (boolean data used only if no set/reset 
	commands or to specify the commands flavors)

